WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:05.880
In recent years the Mandeville community has
changed significantly with large growth in

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.540
small-block rural and residential areas.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.990
In light of this, we are reviewing speed limits
in the area to make sure the community is

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.280
safe and speed limits are consistent and appropriate.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.480
These roads are limited to 50km per hour

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.740
These roads are limited to 70km per hour

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.900
And these two stretches of road are limited
to 80km per hour.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.860
All remaining roads currently have an open
road speed limit of 100km per hour.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.140
There are three areas of interest that we
are focusing on in this review.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.040
Should this section of Tram road have a lower
speed limit?

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.790
Should these lengths of Wards Road, Dawsons
Road and Bradleys Road have lower limits to

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.920
be consistent with McHughs Road and Mandeville
Road?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.090
And should these cul-de-sacs and access roads
have lower speed limits to be consistent with

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.060
the Millfield Subdivision?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.140
We’re holding drop in sessions on these
dates or you can find out more and give us

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:07.760
feedback at Waimakariri.govt.nz/Mandeville.

